From: ITSMEFRTRUST <215584995+ITSMEFRTRUST@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 22:12:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 001/138] Input: drv260x - warn when auto-calibration fails

drv260x_init() waits for the GO bit to clear after starting
auto-calibration, but never checks whether calibration actually
succeeded. When the configured mode does not match the actuator (e.g.
ERM mode on an LRA), the chip sets DIAG_RESULT in the STATUS register,
the driver probes fine, and playback silently produces no vibration.

Read STATUS once calibration completes and warn if DIAG_RESULT is set,
so a misconfigured device tree is visible in the kernel log.

Found while bringing up the DRV2604 on the Apple iPhone 6, where ERM
mode left STATUS at 0x8c (DIAG_RESULT set) and LRA mode gives 0x80.

Fixes: 7132fe4f5687 ("Input: drv260x - add TI drv260x haptics driver")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/input/misc/drv260x.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/input/misc/drv260x.c b/drivers/input/misc/drv260x.c
index 6c5c4c537..93b303105 100644
--- a/drivers/input/misc/drv260x.c
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/drv260x.c
@@ -59,6 +59,9 @@
 
 #define DRV260X_GO_BIT				0x01
 
+/* Status register */
+#define DRV260X_STATUS_DIAG_RESULT	(1 << 3)
+
 /* Library Selection */
 #define DRV260X_LIB_SEL_MASK		0x07
 #define DRV260X_LIB_SEL_RAM			0x0
@@ -423,6 +426,17 @@ static int drv260x_init(struct drv260x_data *haptics)
 		}
 	} while (cal_buf == DRV260X_GO_BIT);
 
+	error = regmap_read(haptics->regmap, DRV260X_STATUS, &cal_buf);
+	if (error) {
+		dev_err(&haptics->client->dev,
+			"Failed to read status register: %d\n", error);
+		return error;
+	}
+
+	if (cal_buf & DRV260X_STATUS_DIAG_RESULT)
+		dev_warn(&haptics->client->dev,
+			 "Auto-calibration failed, check actuator mode and voltages\n");
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
